  1162	    # run.events), then count relay calls whose ts is strictly AFTER it. A post-hoc baseline or a
  1163	    # max-of-all-events anchor would hide a call made between terminal and a later durable event.
  1164	    # LIVENESS GUARD: trust "0 calls after terminal" ONLY if the relay actually captured THIS run —
  1165	    # i.e. it logged >=1 call inside the run window [run_start, terminal]. An empty/stale relay log
  1166	    # (relay not wired) yields a meaningless 0; we OMIT the slice instead (-> fail-closed INVALID in
  1167	    # live mode) so a false 0 can't classify green. Release happens AFTER the grace window so the
  1168	    # token is live during the audited window.
