  1514	def _shell_removes(command: str, norm_path: str) -> bool:
  1515	    """True iff `command` is a PURE ``rm`` that targets `norm_path` EXACTLY.
  1516	
  1517	    Marking a declared file ABSENT is fail-FAST (unsatisfied → hard INVALID), so this must
  1518	    be strict, not fuzzy: the old basename fallback marked the ROOT deliverable absent when
  1519	    an export flow rm'd a COPY (export/index.html) — REL-6 EXPORT class false-INVALID
  1520	    (conv_bc52c276). Now: every token must be rm / a flag / a path (no zip/cp/&&/; compound
  1521	    ops — those go to the fail-safe OPAQUE downgrade instead), and the declared path must
  1522	    match by exact normalized relpath. Anything less certain degrades to present_unproven,
  1523	    which only ever relaxes — never false-INVALIDs."""
