Read-only review completed. Ranked findings:

1. **High: shell opacity can launder stale snapshots into PASS.**  
[harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:1658](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:1658) downgrades every declared file to `present_unproven` for any non-`rm` shell command. Real behavior: write bad final `index.html`, then run `zip site.zip index.html` or `python -m http.server`; a stale snapshot with old good bytes can pass `OutputTruthOracle` at [output_truth.py:188](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/oracles/output_truth.py:188).  
Minimal fix: only downgrade declared paths the shell command can actually mutate; preserve prior `sha` for unaffected paths.

2. **High: `rm` / rename modeling still misses common real deletes.**  
[_shell_removes](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:1514) uses `command.split()` and exact target matching. It misses quoted paths, paths with spaces, `rm -rf parent_dir` deleting `parent_dir/index.html`, and `mv index.html old.html`. False-PASS: stale snapshot still has a deleted declared file and no `absent` gate blocks it.  
Minimal fix: use `shlex.split`, handle `--`, recursive parent containment, and `mv declared elsewhere` as absent.

3. **High: `cancel_at: after_first_file_write` can fire without interrupting a write.**  
[wait_for_first_file_write](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:873) treats any tool not in `_NON_MUTATING_TOOLS` as the trigger, so preview/verify/shell can count; a fast build can also finish before the poll sees the first write, then [run.py:431](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/run.py:431) still lets the kill run. False-PASS in DISCONNECT: the test proves recovery from post-finish kill, not mid-write cancel.  
Minimal fix: trigger only on executed file mutators, and mark INVALID if a build terminal already preceded the kill.

