The draft explicitly notes the gap at [scenarios_rel6_draft.yaml:35](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/scenarios_rel6_draft.yaml:35), while [ExportDownloadOracle](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/oracles/browser_evidence.py:203) skips absent export evidence. Real behavior: model ignores “package as zip”, leaves `index.html` intact, and the api run passes.  
Minimal fix: export scenarios must require an export slice; absent/unrequested export should be INVALID_RUN until API download evidence is wired.

5. **High: product-evidence numeric omissions can pass as zero.**  
[SidecarStopOracle](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/oracles/browser_evidence.py:109) defaults missing `provider_calls_after_terminal` to `0`; [CleanupOracle](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/oracles/browser_evidence.py:233) defaults missing `orphans` to `0`. False-PASS: capture drops the count field but keeps `stopped_at_terminal`/`workspace_released` true.  
Minimal fix: require field presence, not only type when present.

6. **Medium-high: snapshot file cap can omit real declared files.**  
The snapshot walker stops after 2000 files at [disco_api.py:1134](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:1134) and only aliases declared paths already seen at [disco_api.py:1153](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:1153). A legitimate app with `node_modules`/large export output can push `index.html` past the cap and false-FAIL as missing.  
Minimal fix: always stat/read declared paths after the capped walk; prune obvious internal bulk dirs.

7. **Medium: `VERIFIED` is accepted downstream but not terminal in core waits/events.**  
Adapter terminal sets omit `VERIFIED` at [disco_api.py:74](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:74) and [disco_api.py:80](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:80); event terminal status omits it at [events.py:60](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/events.py:60). A product that emits only `VERIFIED` can time out or classify as not finished.  
Minimal fix: add `VERIFIED` consistently to terminal/work-terminal predicates.

8. **Medium: declared path normalization is inconsistent.**  
[_norm_rel](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:1438) handles `./`, but manifest aliasing uses only `lstrip("/")` at [disco_api.py:1153](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:1153), and output existence is exact at [output_truth.py:188](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/oracles/output_truth.py:188). A declared `./index.html` can false-FAIL while `index.html` exists.  
Minimal fix: use the same normalized lookup for aliasing and oracle presence checks.

9. **Medium: zip/binary artifacts are under-adjudicated.**  
[_file_entry](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:1393) records binary content as empty text, while [ExportDownloadOracle](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/oracles/browser_evidence.py:208) only checks nonzero bytes. Correct zip plus `must_contain` can false-FAIL; corrupt nonempty zip can false-PASS.  
Minimal fix: validate zip structure and expected entries for `.zip`/export artifacts.

10. **Medium: orphan attribution still has parallel-run siblings.**  
Scoped counts use substring matching at [run.py:995](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/run.py:995), and volume fallback still uses newly dangling global volumes at [run.py:1234](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/run.py:1234) / [run.py:1254](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/run.py:1254). False-FAIL: unrelated lane creates a dangling volume or ID substring collision. False-PASS: global deltas net to zero while this run leaked.  
Minimal fix: exact name/label matching; in REL-6 parallel mode, no global fallback.

11. **Medium: relay attribution is fail-closed in ways that become false failures under concurrency/shape drift.**  
Unscoped relay records apply to every conversation at [provider_ledger.py:62](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/provider_ledger.py:62); run-time cleanup only accepts numeric `ts` at [run.py:1178](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/run.py:1178). Parallel unscoped post-terminal calls can false-FAIL clean runs; ISO timestamp logs can become false-INVALID missing sidecar/provider evidence.  
Minimal fix: require conversation ids for REL-6 ledgers or isolate relay logs per run; parse ISO timestamps.

12. **Lower but real: follow-up pickup can key on prior finalization noise.**  
[_progress_event_since](/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/harness/build_soak/adapters/disco_api.py:743) accepts any non-user progress after the baseline, not after the newly appended follow-up. A late observation/status from the previous terminalization can cause false pickup, then later timeout/INVALID.  
Minimal fix: wait for the new user-message seq and require pickup evidence after that seq.
